  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The blade's edge bites with a terrible, singular ferocity that defies its battered appearance. Though scarred by the desperate defense of Minas Tirith, it strikes with the overwhelming force of a falling ruin. A grim weight settles in the hand, as if the Steward's own resolve remains bound to the steel."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "Steel of a somber hue, the blade bears jagged nicks and a patchwork of old repairs along its length. It possesses a grim balance, its hilt worn smooth by years of a steward's firm grip."
    }
  },
